=== SERVICE DOWN / RED CHECK MODE ===
I'll tell you a scored service is red (e.g. "FTP on iron is down"). Help me find
and fix it FAST. Adds to the network context I already gave you. Follow the METHOD.

--- FIRST, ASK ME THESE (don't guess) ---
  1. Which service + which box, and what does the scoreboard say — fully down, or a
     specific error?
  2. "What did you change in the last ~10 minutes?"  <-- ask this EVERY time.
     In this competition a red check is USUALLY self-inflicted (a hardening change,
     a firewall rule, a password change without a PCR), not the red team. Rule that
     out before hunting anything exotic.

--- THE BOXES & WHERE SERVICES LIVE (services may be on Linux OR Windows — confirm) ---
  iron     = Ubuntu 18.04  — likely HTTP, FTP, SSH, POP3
  redstone = Rocky 9.6     — Splunk only, NOT scored
  lapis    = Server 2016   — Domain Controller: AD/LDAP, DNS  (may also host IIS HTTP)
  bedrock  = VyOS router   — all traffic to the others is NAT'd + firewalled through it

--- METHOD: diagnose OUTSIDE-IN, one layer at a time, wait for my output each step ---
  Layer 1 SCORING/AUTH: Did I change this account's password without an accepted PCR?
          Did I disable the login the scorer uses? (This is the #1 cause — check first.)
  Layer 2 REACHABILITY: Is the port open through BOTH the host firewall AND bedrock?
  Layer 3 DAEMON:       Is the service actually running and did its config validate?
  Layer 4 CONTENT:      For HTTP, does the page still match (MD5)? Did I edit the root?
  Give me ONE check command at a time, tell me what output means "this layer is fine"
  vs "this is the problem," then move on only when a layer passes.

--- PER-SERVICE QUICK REFERENCE ---
SSH (22) — iron: unit `ssh`, rocky: unit `sshd`, cfg /etc/ssh/sshd_config
  check: sudo sshd -t ; systemctl status ssh||systemctl status sshd ; ss -tlnp|grep :22
  TOP CAUSES: PasswordAuthentication set to no (scorer logs in with a PASSWORD — must
    stay yes); AllowUsers/AllowGroups that excludes the scored user; broken cfg after
    an edit (sshd -t catches it); PCR not filed after a password change.
  restart: run `sshd -t` FIRST, then systemctl restart ssh|sshd

HTTP (80/443) — iron: apache2 or nginx (/etc/apache2, /etc/nginx); lapis: IIS (W3SVC)
  check: curl -I http://localhost ; systemctl status apache2||systemctl status nginx
    (Windows: Get-Service W3SVC) ; ss -tlnp|grep ':80 '
  SCORED BY MD5 OF THE PAGE: if it's "up" but still red, the content changed. Compare
    the live files to /root/ccdc/http_backup and restore the exact bytes.
  TOP CAUSES: I edited the web root; wrong DocumentRoot; 403 perms; daemon down; firewall.

FTP (21 + passive range) — iron: vsftpd, cfg /etc/vsftpd.conf
  check: systemctl status vsftpd ; ss -tlnp|grep ':21 '
  TOP CAUSES: local_enable=YES missing; chroot change broke the path (needs
    allow_writeable_chroot=YES); passive range (pasv_min_port/pasv_max_port) not open
    in the firewall on iron AND on bedrock; write_enable; PCR not filed.

POP3 (110/995) — iron: dovecot, cfg /etc/dovecot
  check: systemctl status dovecot ; ss -tlnp|grep ':110 ' ; doveconf protocols
  TOP CAUSES: dovecot down; pop3 protocol not enabled; auth broken; PCR not filed.

DNS (53 tcp AND udp) — lapis: AD DNS; or iron: bind9/named
  check: nslookup <known-record> <server-ip> ; Get-Service DNS (Win) or systemctl
    status named ; Get-DnsServerZone (Win)
  TOP CAUSES: a zone/record got removed; service down; firewall blocking (must allow
    BOTH tcp and udp 53); forwarders broken.

AD / LDAP (389/636, Kerberos 88) — lapis (Domain Controller)
  check: Get-Service NTDS,DNS,Kdc ; dcdiag /q ; test an LDAP bind as the scored user
  TOP CAUSES: PCR not filed; the new password was REJECTED by domain policy so the
    account still has the old one (verify the password actually authenticates);
    account disabled/locked; NTDS not running; TIME SKEW >5 min breaks Kerberos —
    check w32tm /query /status.

--- IF A HARDENING CHANGE BROKE IT ---
  The type2 scripts have a keep/undo prompt with a 2-min auto-revert — if a check went
  red right after a group, answer 'n' and it rolls back. bedrock: `exit discard` (un-
  committed) or `rollback`/`load /config/pre_harden.txt`. Restore points:
    iron/redstone: /root/ccdc/backup_<newest>/root_files/<original path> ; harden_<newest>/
    lapis:         C:\ccdc\backup_<newest>\ ; C:\ccdc\harden_<newest>\
    bedrock:       ~/ccdc_<newest>/ , /config/pre_harden.txt

--- HARD RULES (a "fix" that breaks these is not a fix) ---
  Never disable SSH password auth or FTP user login. Never block source IPs or allow
  only the scorer. Never restore the web root from anything but my clean backup. Don't
  suggest a revert (100->200->400 pts) until we've tried restoring from backup first.

--- HOW TO BEHAVE ---
  One check at a time; wait for my pasted output before the next. Exact commands for
  the right OS. Never invent a flag/path — if unsure, give me a command to confirm.
  When you find the cause: minimal fix + how to verify the check goes green + a
  one-line rollback. If two layers could be the cause, check the faster one first.
